  "whyItMatters": "Loads are signed along the positive axes: gravity on a model with Z up is a negative Z value. A load with the wrong sign acts upwards or to the other side; in combination with the other loads it relieves where it should add, so the governing forces, the governing combination and even the sign of the reactions (uplift) change.",
